 As I say, I garee with the non-separation of .iseri'abo.  As for "le mi
cukta", while I hear what you are saying, don't forget that it really is
a shorthand way of saying "le cukta pe mi".  "mi" doesn't really modify
cukta in the same way that it would in "le me mi cukta" or "le mi zei
cukta", although it doesn't hurt to think of it your way.  On the other
hand, I wouldn't take out the space between the le's in "le le gerku ku
bongu", either (although legally I could).

=20

             --gy

